---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
const pageTitle = "George's Home";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <main>
    <Prose>
      <p>
        When I was 10yo I went to an informatics class with a friend and fell in
        love with computers. It was love at first keystroke. Two years later I
        learned my first programming language: Visual Basic <Icon
          class="inline"
          name="fa7-brands:microsoft"
          size={16}
        />. I also figured out how to assemble and disassemble computers and
        earned a lot of money for a 12yo. The year was 2005, the beginning of my
        career 😂.
      </p>
      <p>
        Down the line I got a BS in Information Systems, but at some point when
        I got asked what I wanted to be when I grew up I responded:
        "Scientist!!!". Poor choice in terms of finances, good one in terms of
        passion. Later on I got an MS in Computer Science.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am originally from Brazil 🇧🇷, but when I moved to the US 🇺🇸 in 2018,
        it was the beginning of the Deep Learning boom. Word2Vec had been
        published 5 years earlier, and everyone was working on something that
        stacked on top of it. The Transformers paper had been published a year
        before I moved. I did not know TensorFlow, and Hugging Face's
        Transformers library did not exist yet, so I spent a few weeks writing
        my own from scratch. Pretty fun times. I am currently in Belgium 🇧🇪,
        still tinkering with computers, and still working in research.
      </p>
      <p>On this website, I document some of the things I learn and do.</p>
    </Prose>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
